 Next: [Talk, type, and interrupt](using-gadget.md). For configuration details and plugin development, read [Hermes integration](hermes-integration.md).
+
+Optional Wear pet delivery: set `platforms.gadget.extra.enable_pets: true` and use
+an approved client advertising `caps.pet.asset_channel: 4`. The current profile's
+active pet is converted to PNG with alpha. Pillow is optional; unavailable or invalid
+pet art leaves conversations working. See the [pet wire contract](protocol.md#optional-pet-assets-wear-extension).
+This is an opt-in extension; no personal art is bundled with the plugin.
diff --git a/docs/protocol.md b/docs/protocol.md
index 886197e..47c1390 100644
--- a/docs/protocol.md
+++ b/docs/protocol.md
@@ -230,3 +230,32 @@ mac = HMAC-SHA256(key, "hermes-gadget/v1|ota|" + device_id + "|" + nonce + "|" +
 - `proto` is a single integer, and a server rejects versions it does not speak.
 - Adding optional fields or new message types does not change the version. Receivers ignore unknown types and fields.
 - Changing the meaning of an existing field does.
+
+### Optional pet assets (Wear extension)
+
+Disabled by default (`platforms.gadget.extra.enable_pets: true` opts in). An
+approved device advertises `caps.pet.asset_channel: 4` and sends `pet.request`
+after pairing. Unknown requests remain ignorable. No conversation waits for pets.
+The adapter resolves the active pet in its current Hermes profile home, respecting
+`display.pet.enabled` and `display.pet.slug`. Missing Pillow/pet configuration or
+invalid art returns `pet.unavailable`, without paths or error details.
+
+`pet.manifest` contains `slug`, `name`, `cell_width:192`, `cell_height:208`,
+`loop_ms:1100`, and one or two `sheets`. Each sheet has `kind` (`base` or
+`companion`), lowercase SHA-256, compressed `bytes`, `width`, `height`, and `rows`
+with `name`, zero-based `index`, and occupied `frames`. Use at most six base
+frames, trimming transparent tails. Base row taxonomy follows the current/legacy
+Hermes grid; the base atlas is never extended. Optional `gadgetSheet` in pet.json
+references a separate asset and explicit listening/talking/sleeping rows. Talking
+requires three occupied mouth poses. This metadata remains a Hermes-side proposal.
+
+For each PNG: `asset.start {stream,sha256,bytes,format:"png"}`, ordered binary
+channel `0x04` packets (normal four-byte header; seq starts at zero, chunks at most
+4096 bytes), then `asset.end {stream}`. `asset.abort {stream}` discards a partial
+transfer; disappearance, revocation or error also invalidates it. Verify exact
+length/hash before promotion, never use slug or supplied paths as cache filenames.
+Limit two assets, 2 MiB compressed each, 3.2 million pixels per asset, grid dimensions
+192..1728 by 208..2496 divisible by cell size, and 15 seconds of transfer inactivity.
+The reference server paces chunks at 20 ms and caps the entire delivery at 30 seconds.
+Metadata paths and symlinks must stay within the profile pet directory. RGB565 image
+channel 2 is unchanged. PNG preserves alpha; no new native Python dependency is needed.
